{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DFVaiEGSXDeC9EfSXH6nVb","type":"tool_result","content":"# Plan for #204\n\n## Implementation\n\nScope: PR 1 only (filing rules for LLM scanners, pure, inside `internal/config`, `internal/scanner` and `internal/scanner/stale`). PRs 2 to 4 of the issue's plan (executor output dir, agent adapter, `AgentEngine`, serve wiring, `CLAUDE.md`) are human-led and are not part of this plan. Do not touch them, `.ard/config.yaml`, `.ard/scanners/`, `.github/` or `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nChecked against main (`1ba5310`). Already landed from #215, so do NOT redo: `config.Route` (`RoutePending/None/NeedsHuman`, `types.go:72`), the LLM default `RouteNone` and the \"LLM scanners may not use pending\" config error (`load.go:179-187`, `load.go:398-403`), `routeLabel` and `execution.roleLabels` (`pipeline.go:76`, `:490`), the route-aware `joinableIssue(lbls, scanner, routeLbl, p, group)` (`pipeline.go:511`) and the pre-filing guard (`CheckFindings`, `guard.go`, placed after the scan in `Pipeline.Run`). The join-rule and filing-labels contract in the issue is therefore already satisfied; keep `joinableIssue` as is and only add tests (Step 9).\n\n### Steps\n\n1. `internal/config/types.go`: add `func (r Role) LLMScanner() bool { return r.Kind == KindScanner && r.ScanPath == \"\" }`. Change `ReadsUntrusted` (line 164) to `r.Kind != KindScanner || r.LLMScanner()`. No behaviour change. Reason: one definition of \"LLM scanner\" for the later checks.\n2. `internal/config/load.go`, `applyOverride` (autoclose branch, line ~394): when `*ov.autoclose` is true and `role.LLMScanner()`, append `&Error{File: cfgPath, Key: keyRef + \".autoclose\", Msg: \"an LLM scanner never closes an issue for absence; autoclose is valid only for a scanner with a scan executable\"}`. The default (false, line 183) stays.\n3. `internal/config/load.go`, `applyOverrides`: after the overrides loop (before the plan_section ownership check), for every role with `LLMScanner()` append an `*Error` (Key `overrideKeyRef(\"scanners/\"+name)+\".max_budget_usd\"`) when `MaxBudgetUSD <= 0`, and another (Key `….every`) when `Every < 24*time.Hour`. Messages name the key and the floor. This runs in the load path that both `ard config check` and serve use, so both report it. Existing LLM-scanner fixtures (`internal/config/load_test.go`, `internal/servecmd/cfgloader_test.go:39`, `internal/servecmd/rebuild_test.go:26`, any `testdata`) will now need `max_budget_usd` and `every: 24h` or more; update them.\n4. `internal/scanner/llm.go` (new, pure): `func ParseLLMFingerprint(fp string) (rule, path, symbol string, ok bool)` and `func CheckLLMFingerprints(fs []Finding, exists func(path string) bool) DecodeErrors`, per the issue's grammar: split on `:` into 2 or 3 non-empty fields; rule `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}$`; path `^[A-Za-z0-9._/@+-]+$`, `path.Clean(p)==p`, not absolute, no `..` segment, not `.`; symbol `^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_./-]{0,127}$`. `CheckLLMFingerprints` also requires the path to be in `f.Files` and `exists(path)`. Errors are `DecodeError{Line: 1-based finding index, Msg: fixed text}` (at most 20, like `maxErrorLines` in `finding.go`); `Msg` never contains the fingerprint or any finding text. The 512-byte cap already lives in `DecodeFindings`.\n5. `internal/scanner/neardup.go` (new, pure): `const NearDupThreshold = 0.8`; `type TitledIssue struct{ Number int; Titles []string }`; `type NearDup struct{ Fingerprint string; Issue int }`; `func SimilarTitles(a, b string) bool`; `func SkipNearDuplicates(items []Item, open []TitledIssue) (kept []Item, dups []NearDup)`. Normalise: lowercase, every rune outside `[a-z0-9]` becomes a space, drop one-character tokens and the stop list `a an and for in is of on the to with`; compare as sets; equal non-empty sets match, otherwise both sets need at least 3 tokens and Jaccard >= 0.8; an empty set never matches. Walk items in `lessItem` order (`group.go:34`, most severe first); compare each against every open issue (`Number` > 0) and against earlier kept items of the run (`NearDup.Issue == 0`). A skipped item is not recorded as a row.\n6. `internal/scanner/pipeline.go`: add `Title string` to `IssueView` and fill it from `is.Title` at line 199. Add `NearDup int` to `RunResult` and `\"near_duplicates\", res.NearDup` to the `scanner.run` log in `record`. In `Run`, after `items` is built (line ~373) and before `PlanGroups`, only when `role.LLMScanner()`: build `[]TitledIssue` from `views` (`v.Title` plus every `v.Parsed.Lines[i].Title`; check the `Line` field name in `marker.go`), call `SkipNearDuplicates`, set `res.NearDup`, and log one `scanner.near_duplicate` (`fingerprint`, `issue`) per skip. Comment that dry-run synthetic issues carry no title and are not compared.\n7. `internal/scanner/pipeline.go`, footer: add `const llmFooter = \"Filed by an LLM scanner; not triaged automatically. Add `ard:pending` to send it to triage, or close it as not planned to dismiss it for 90 days.\"` In `create` (line ~838), when `e.role.Route != config.RoutePending`, append `\"\\n\\n\" + llmFooter + \"\\n\"` to the rendered body after `RenderBody`. Make sure a later join (which re-renders with `prev` = existing body) keeps the footer and does not duplicate it, and that `issueMD`'s rendering is unaffected. A deterministic `route: pending` issue gets no footer.\n8. Grammar-failure logging: add to `internal/scanner/llm.go` a helper `func LLMGrammarLines(errs DecodeErrors) string` (fixed text \"invalid findings at lines 3, 7 (and N more)\") for the later engine. No engine exists yet in PR 1, so nothing calls `CheckLLMFingerprints` in `Run`; do not wire it into `Pipeline.Run`.\n9. `internal/scanner/stale/stale.go` and `decide.go` (owner comment: widen the stale closer): an open issue that has the `ard:scanner:<name>` label and no other `ard:` label (the `route: none` state) is now a candidate too. In `precheck` (decide.go:64) replace `!hasLabel(is, labels.Pending)` with a helper `staleCandidate(is)`: true when it has `ard:pending`, or when its only `ard:`-prefixed label (case-insensitive) is the scanner label. All later rules (hold, needs-human, running, human author, too new, linked PR, activity) are unchanged. In `run`, the search currently asks for `label:\"ard:pending\"`: keep that query and add one query per configured scanner name, `is:open label:\"ard:scanner:<name>\" -label:\"ard:needs-human\" -label:\"ard:hold\"` (one `SearchIssues` call each, results merged and de-duplicated by number), because a search cannot match \"no other ard: label\". The re-fetch/precheck path in `one` already rechecks labels.\n\n### Test plan\n\nCommand: `make lint test` (or `go test ./internal/config/... ./internal/scanner/... ./internal/servecmd/...` while iterating).\n\n- `internal/config/load_test.go` (table): LLM scanner with `autoclose: true` is an error, with `false` valid; deterministic scanner with `true` valid; LLM default is false; `LLMScanner()` true only for a prompt scanner (a `ScanPath` scanner, a triage role: false); LLM scanner without `max_budget_usd` errors; `every: 12h` errors; valid LLM scanner (`max_budget_usd: 2`, `every: 72h`) loads clean; `route: pending` on an LLM scanner still errors (existing). `ard config check` path: one test through the check command's loader (find it under `internal/cli` or `cmd`) that the errors are reported; `internal/servecmd/cfgloader_test.go`: serve's loader reports the same.\n- `internal/scanner/llm_test.go`: valid `adr-0007:internal/foo/bar.go:Server.Start` and a directory `invariant-3:internal/committer`; invalid: spaces, uppercase rule, `../x`, leading `/`, path not in `files`, path missing (exists false), symbol starting with a digit, empty field, over 512 bytes (via the fingerprint length the helper sees), `:` in path, four fields; no `Msg` contains the planted fingerprint; at most 20 errors; `LLMGrammarLines` text.\n- `internal/scanner/neardup_test.go`: equal short sets match; \"label\" vs \"labels\"