{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLZBFk9oYphgrnNKnJWV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UMGL8iRLEnv4C2CYhF4K7R","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='docs/proposal.md'\nL=open(p).read().split('\\n')\ni=next(n for n,l in enumerate(L) if l.startswith('**The pre-filing guard cannot be turned off.**'))\npara=\"**LLM scanners (`prompt.txt`) file under extra rules.** `autoclose: true` on one is a config error: an LLM scanner never closes an issue for absence. `every` defaults to at least 24h and a value below 24h is an error; `max_budget_usd`, when set, must be above 0. An LLM fingerprint is `rule:path` or `rule:path:symbol` (rule `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,63}`, a clean relative path without `..` that is also listed in the finding's `files` and exists, symbol `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_./-]{0,127}`); a bad fingerprint is reported by finding index only, never by content. Before grouping, a finding whose title is a near-duplicate of an open issue's title or checklist line, or of a more severe finding in the same run, is skipped without a ledger row, so it is offered again next run. Titles are lowercased, reduced to `[a-z0-9]` tokens, minus one-character tokens and a short stop list; they match when the token sets are equal, or when both have at least three tokens and their Jaccard similarity is at least 0.8. An issue filed by a scanner whose route is not `pending` ends with a footer explaining that a human adds `ard:pending` to send it to triage or closes it as not planned to dismiss it. The stale closer also considers an open issue whose only `ard:` label is its scanner label (route `none`). The engine that runs `prompt.txt` scanners is not wired in yet.\"\nL.insert(i+1,'')\nL.insert(i+2,para)\nopen(p,'w').write('\\n'.join(L))\nE\ngit -c core.excludesFile=/dev/null status --porcelain --untracked-files=all | grep -v \"^?? .ard-input\""},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"