{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLZC9inU5oUrtP7TejQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR 1 of the LLM scanner engine is done: the filing rules for `prompt.txt` scanners. No LLM scanner runs yet, because the skip in `Pipeline.Run` is still in place. `go test ./...` passes and `go vet` is clean. `make lint` also runs gofmt, which trips on `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`; this change does not touch that file.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Config:** `autoclose: true` on an LLM scanner is now an error, as is `every` below 24h or an explicit `max_budget_usd` of 0 or less.\n- **Fingerprints:** new `rule:path[:symbol]` checking in `internal/scanner/llm.go`. Errors name the finding index only, never its content. It is not called from `Run` yet.\n- **Near-duplicates:** `internal/scanner/neardup.go` skips an LLM finding whose title is close to an open issue's, or to a more severe finding in the same run. Skipped findings get no ledger row, so they are offered again next run.\n- **Footer:** an issue created by a scanner whose route is not `pending` ends with the LLM footer, and a join keeps exactly one.\n- **Stale closer:** an issue whose only `ard:` label is its scanner label is now a candidate, with one extra search per scanner.\n- **Docs:** one paragraph in `docs/proposal.md`.\n\nA few things differ from the plan:\n- **Budget check:** I did not add \"no `max_budget_usd` is an error\". A role inherits the global budget, which is already validated, so it is never missing.\n- **`every` default:** a short `every` is raised to 24h rather than rejected, so existing configs still load. Only an explicit value below 24h errors. `TestLoadOverrides` and `testdata/resolved.golden` were updated to expect the 24h floor.\n- **Hold and needs-human:** a scanner-only issue that also has `ard:hold` or `ard:needs-human` is now \"not a candidate\" rather than \"hold\" or \"needs-human\". It is skipped either way.\n- **Tests:** near-duplicate skipping and the footer are tested through helpers (`SkipNearDuplicates`, `createBody`), because `Run` still skips LLM scanners. I added no separate serve or `ard config check` test, since both use the same loader, which the `internal/config` tests cover.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/204/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1093,"cache_read_input_tokens":66648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1093},"output_tokens":764,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2a8bf32-d6e4-436f-a631-72cb4dc75f8f","uuid":"2b0ae1bd-21a6-4d91-afa6-f27357503633","timestamp":"2026-11-23T21:17:52.679Z","request_id":"req_011ChLZC9acRfNPVkr4oTn6A"}
